Dear Priya,

We are requesting a Fitness-for-Service assessment from CIE regarding localized metal loss on line 4-RA-101 in the ATU-100. As documented in QSCP-NCR-2024-031, a reading at 4-RA-101-06 was recorded at 3.59 mm, which is below the 3.81 mm t-min for this rich amine service. Subsequent PAUT corrosion mapping detailed in LNDE-RPT-20241202-036-R0 confirmed a minimum thickness of 3.55 mm at the elbow.

Please evaluate the remaining strength of this component based on the design conditions of 862 kPa(g) and 82 °C. We require your recommendation on the suitability for continued operation until the next planned outage. Please address the submittal to Priya Natarajan for formal review.

Jennifer Walsh

